  "articleBody": "While simple quarter-round can be a manageable weekend project, complex architectural millwork demands precision tools, sharp blades, and deep field experience. Here is when to bring in an experienced finish carpenter:\n\n- Installing pre-hung or custom interior doors: Plumbing jambs, creating consistent margins, and setting strikes on out-of-square framing requires advanced shimming and scribing.\n- Installing crown molding along uneven ceilings: Compound miters, coped internal corners, and rolling ceiling transitions demand precision cutting to avoid wide, sagging joints.\n- Scribing built-ins, shelving, or baseboards to wavy drywall: When walls curve or floors pitch, standard butt joints fail. Scribing ensures materials follow the profile neatly.\n- Working with expensive hardwood or paint-grade materials: Miscuts on high-end profiles turn costly very quickly. A professional ensures efficient material yield and exact cuts.\n- Multi-room trim updates requiring coordinated painting: Managing transitions, hardware clearances, and paint-ready surface prep across several rooms works best under one cohesive crew.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps: Abraham Becerra leads HH Remodeling LLC as a hands-on general contractor, personally handling finish carpentry, molding, drywall, and interior painting throughout Aurora and the greater Denver region. Call 303-505-0866 to get your trim project scheduled.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
